---
source: crates/ccusage-cli-parser/src/tests.rs
expression: "help_text_for_args(&[\"ccusage\".to_string(), \"sync\".to_string(),\n\"setup\".to_string(),])"
---
Configure the bucket, credentials, and identity.

USAGE:
  ccusage sync setup <OPTIONS>

OPTIONS:
  --provider <provider>                Where usage is stored: a Google Cloud bucket, a local directory, or a hub reached over HTTP (default: gcs, choices: gcs | fs | http)
  -p, --project <project>              Cloud project that owns the bucket (default: discovered)
  --bucket <bucket>                    Bucket to sync into (default: created for you)
  --dir <dir>                          Directory to keep usage in (fs provider)
  --url <url>                          Address of a 'ccusage sync serve' hub (http provider); the bearer token is read from CCUSAGE_SYNC_TOKEN
  --machine-id <id>                    Sync as this machine id instead of minting one (default: minted)
  --machine-label <label>              Name the dashboard shows for this machine (default: none)
  --location <location>                Location for a bucket ccusage creates (default: project default)
  --prefix <prefix>                    Key prefix inside the bucket (default: ccusage/v1)
  --auth <auth>                        Credential source to configure (default: auto, choices: auto | adc | hmac)
  --non-interactive                    Never prompt; fail instead of asking a question (default: false)
  --recreate                           Replace the configured bucket instead of reusing it (default: false)
  -j, --json                           Output in JSON format (default: false)
  --config <config>                    Path to configuration file (default: auto-discovery)
  -h, --help                           Display this help message
